# Line endings.
#
# The migration files are read by the test suite and sent to PostgreSQL as
# one string. A Windows checkout converts a text file to CRLF by default, and
# a stray carriage return inside a dollar quoted function body becomes part of
# the body rather than ending the line. The failure that follows names a
# syntax error in SQL that is correct on disk, which sends the reader looking
# in the wrong file.
#
# Pin the text files to LF on every platform. This is not a preference about
# editors. It is the condition under which the suite means anything on
# Windows.
*.go text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.proto text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
# The mark is compiled into the server binary and served from it, so a line
# ending conversion changes the bytes that reach a browser.
*.svg text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Generated code.
#
# Marking the generated protobuf files keeps them out of a diff by default and
# out of the language statistics. They are still committed, and CI regenerates
# them and fails on a difference, because the last version of this repository
# carried hand written files that claimed to be generated.
internal/quorrapb/*.pb.go linguist-generated=true

# Binary, and never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
